# Copy to .env and uncomment one provider block.
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL is <provider>:<model-id>, split on the first colon.
# Defaults to anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6.

# --- Anthropic ---------------------------------------------------------------
SHANNON_AI_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
SHANNON_AI_MODEL=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=your-oauth-token-here

# --- OpenAI ------------------------------------------------------------------
# SHANNON_AI_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL=openai:gpt-5.5

# --- xAI ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# SHANNON_AI_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL=xai:grok-4.5

# --- AWS Bedrock -------------------------------------------------------------
# Bearer token only; model must be enabled in your region.
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=your-bearer-token
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL=amazon-bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8

# --- Custom Base URL ---------------------------------------------------------
# Route through a proxy or gateway (LiteLLM, an internal endpoint).
# Pick the block matching the API dialect your gateway speaks, and uncomment all
# three lines. The provider prefix picks the dialect; the model id is whatever
# name your gateway serves it under.

# Anthropic compatible - Anthropic Messages:
# SHANNON_AI_API_KEY=your-gateway-key-here
# SHANNON_AI_BASE_URL=https://llm-gateway.example.com
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6

# OpenAI compatible - Chat Completions (default) or Responses:
# SHANNON_AI_API_KEY=your-gateway-key-here
# SHANNON_AI_BASE_URL=https://llm-gateway.example.com/v1
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL=openai:gpt-5.5
# SHANNON_AI_OPENAI_FORMAT=responses

# --- Other provider ----------------------------------------------------------
# Any other provider the Pi harness supports. Name it in SHANNON_AI_MODEL and
# supply the key via the generic SHANNON_AI_API_KEY. Pi validates the provider
# and model at preflight.
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL=openrouter:moonshotai/kimi-k3
# SHANNON_AI_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# --- Misc --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Forward /etc/hosts entries into the worker container.
# SHANNON_FORWARD_HOSTS=false

# See the guide below to use an OpenAI subscription
# https://github.com/KeygraphHQ/shannon/blob/main/docs/ai-providers.md#openai-codex-chatgpt-pluspro-subscription
# SHANNON_USE_PI_AUTH=1
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5

# Or the guide below to use an xAI subscription
# https://github.com/KeygraphHQ/shannon/blob/main/docs/ai-providers.md#xai-grok-subscription
# SHANNON_USE_PI_AUTH=1
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL=xai:grok-4.6

# --- Fork additions (Corvus) --------------------------------------------------
# Host-side Temporal gRPC address. Set when the compose file's published port is
# remapped (this fork remaps it to 127.0.0.1:7234 to leave 7233 free for another
# Temporal deployment on the same host).
# TEMPORAL_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:7234
#
# Opt in to running the CLI as root/sudo. Off by default: upstream refuses root
# because bind-mounted workspace and report files come back owned by root. Only
# set this in deployments where the CLI is spawned by a service that already runs
# as root and the operator owns the file-ownership trade-off.
# SHANNON_ALLOW_ROOT=1
#
# Context window and output ceiling advertised for a gateway model the Pi
# catalogue does not know (e.g. SHANNON_AI_MODEL=openai:z-ai/glm-5.3 with a
# custom SHANNON_AI_BASE_URL). An unknown id borrows a reference descriptor,
# and Pi clamps each request's output budget to the borrowed window; defaults
# are generous because the serving endpoint enforces the real limit. Override
# only when the gateway model genuinely has a small window. Both must be
# positive integers.
# SHANNON_AI_CONTEXT_WINDOW=200000
# SHANNON_AI_MAX_TOKENS=32768
#
# --- Fork additions (Corvus): per-stage model routing ------------------------
# Override the model for individual pipeline stages. A stage is an agent name
# (PRE_RECON, RECON, INJECTION_VULN, XSS_VULN, AUTH_VULN, AUTHZ_VULN,
# SSRF_VULN, INJECTION_EXPLOIT, XSS_EXPLOIT, AUTH_EXPLOIT, AUTHZ_EXPLOIT,
# MISCELLANEOUS_EXPLOIT, REPORT, VALIDATE_AUTHENTICATION) or a model role
# (SMALL, MEDIUM, LARGE — the structured-generation / task-formation / SAST
# seams). Same "<provider>:<model-id>" shape as SHANNON_AI_MODEL; a stage
# without an override falls back to it. Both CLI and worker fail loud on a
# near-miss (lower-case suffix, missing provider) instead of routing nothing.
# Example: cheap recon, strong exploitation:
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL_RECON=openai:z-ai/glm-5.3-flash
# SHANNON_AI_MODEL_INJECTION_EXPLOIT=openai:z-ai/glm-5.3
#
# Per-stage output budget (tokens), replacing the model's advertised ceiling
# for that stage only. Useful to cap a verbose cheap stage or widen a
# reasoning-heavy one. Positive integers; garbage fails loud.
# SHANNON_AI_MAX_TOKENS_REPORT=8192
#
# --- Fork additions (Corvus): spend ceiling (budget in the scan config YAML) --
# The ceiling itself is config, not env: a scan's YAML may set
#   budget: { max_usd: "5.00", max_prompt_tokens: "1000000" }
# (either bound alone works; both are positive numbers). When the accumulated
# spend — every agent's and operational metric's cost, and every request's
# input+cache-read+cache-write tokens — reaches either bound, the pipeline stops
# starting new analysis work and ends "partial" with the reason
# budget_exhausted, never a silent "completed". Findings proven before the
# ceiling stay in the report; resuming the workspace with a higher ceiling
# retries the skipped work.
#
# A USD bound only counts spend the harness can price. A gateway model
# (SHANNON_AI_BASE_URL set) has no price unless you declare one:
# SHANNON_AI_PRICE_INPUT_<MODEL>=0.60
# SHANNON_AI_PRICE_OUTPUT_<MODEL>=2.20
# <MODEL> is the model id upper-cased with non-alphanumerics folded to _
# (z-ai/glm-5.3 -> Z_AI_GLM_5_3). Rates are USD per 1M tokens, plain decimals.
# The pair must be complete — one side alone fails loud — and preflight warns
# when a USD ceiling is set but a selected gateway model has no price (its
# spend would stay zero and the ceiling would not count it). Cache reads and
# writes are priced at zero; if the gateway charges for cache, blend that into
# the input rate.
# SHANNON_AI_PRICE_INPUT_Z_AI_GLM_5_3=0.60
# SHANNON_AI_PRICE_OUTPUT_Z_AI_GLM_5_3=2.20

# --- Fork additions (Corvus): governed egress -------------------------------
# Setting this variable routes the whole scan through an enforcing forward
# proxy (the Corvus EnforcingProxy re-checks every CONNECT and every
# absolute-form request against the scan's frozen scope):
#   - every agent browser launches with --proxy-server (playwright config)
#   - HTTP_PROXY/HTTPS_PROXY (both letter cases) reach the scan container so
#     env-honoring clients (curl, wget, requests…) are governed too — curl
#     reads only lowercase http_proxy for plain-http URLs, which is why both
#     spellings are forwarded
#   - NO_PROXY/no_proxy carry exactly the infrastructure hosts (loopback, the
#     shannon-temporal control plane, and the LLM gateway host when
#     SHANNON_AI_BASE_URL names one) — an allowlist, never empty and never
#     an escape hatch: the scan target is governed, the worker's own control
#     plane is not
#   - host /etc/hosts forwarding is disabled for the run, whatever
#     SHANNON_FORWARD_HOSTS says (extra name->IP mappings would hand the
#     container resolution paths the proxy never sees)
# The URL must be a bare http(s) URL — a typo fails loud before any Docker
# work. Honest residual: raw sockets (curl --noproxy, bash /dev/tcp) do not
# honor proxy variables and bypass the gate; per-request visibility inside a
# tunnel needs an explicit MITM, documented as a follow-up. LLM gateway
# traffic (SHANNON_AI_BASE_URL) is deliberately not proxied: Node's fetch
# ignores these variables, and the gateway is infrastructure, never the scan
# target.
# SHANNON_PROXY_URL=http://172.18.0.1:9400
